  "needs_review": null,
  "story": {
    "who": "Satnam Sokhal, a chess player and teacher from the area, joins the museum's Play Champions. The museum's own website says he has played since he was nine, was called up to play for East London against teams from other counties, and enjoys teaching children and adults alike.",
    "then": "The sessions are part of Young V&A's Power of Play programme, which the museum's website describes as a consortium bringing learning through play to children in Tower Hamlets. The LEGO Foundation funds it and the LEGO Group in London coordinates it.",
    "now": "One session is a chess day with plenty of sets, including a giant one, and a black-and-white play kit made for the youngest children. The museum says beginners, experienced players and the curious are all welcome.",
    "vibe": "The museum's own website describes a team of friendly Play Champions leading play adventures in the interactive galleries and on Town Square. The activities rotate between the Play, Imagine and Design Galleries.",
    "worth_knowing": [
      "Adults are required to take part alongside their children at every Play Saturdays activity.",
      "Young V&A shares the Power of Play project with several partners, among them Save the Children and EasyPeasy."
    ],
